tion/issues/928-requirements.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner (those added since the 2026-10-26 boundary review)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. This is the owner-facing list Goal 5 requires. R-13 accepted the earlier list, so only decisions recorded after that review are listed here. Each is recorded in the plan's 'Decisions made mid-build', and each was settled as follows. (1) The unknown-host Stop block is recorded as gate `host` (`unknown-host`, since 3.8.0), settled by making it countable like every other block. (2) If host.py fails to load, the Stop exits 1 through main's floor and does not block, settled by R-2 (a fallback would read host variables outside the seam). (3) fields_present and event wait for #1038's doctor detection as their reader, settled by #1037 asking for null to be kept apart from absent; the owner can veto. (4) Pre-switch pass, at the owner's request for high confidence: PRAWDUCT_HOST is case-insensitive; the sweep covers linked worktrees, non-git directories and other interpreters; the digest names an unresolvable project dir. (5) The adversarial review's mixed-version window (an old script with a new lib, or the reverse, loses the Stop deferrals and can drop one clear-verdict block) is handled only by operator guidance: 'switch the live checkout while no session is mid-Stop'. That guidance lives only in the plan, which archives at release, and not in the change fragment. Whoever advances prawduct-live after the merge should read it there. (6) The release plan adds host-seam as a v3.8.0 release requirement. It cites an owner ruling of 2026-10-21 on #1037 and a confirmation on 2026-10-28; the witness is the external issue, not this branch. Alignment-pass misses: none observed. Every capability traces to #1037 or the owner's parity request (scope-trace clean apart from fields_present/event, which are accepted priors).", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts